}

^["risk_model"]{
 hard_failures: [
  "a move leaves refs or lineage strings pointing at the dated cut or the old shelf folders",
  "the snapshot tag names a commit whose cut differs from the shelved one",
  "a mechanical pass rewrites a claim statement or renames an anchor"
 ]
 soft_failures: [
  "LSP and graph caches keep the old paths until reindexed",
  "open worktrees and plan streams still name the old paths"
 ]
 recoveries: [
  "spw resolve and the cut gate run after every commit; any new unresolved ref blocks the commit",
  "plan streams are history and keep the old paths; cards and roots follow the move",
  "the tag caches-cut/2026.09.30 holds the layout as shelved, so any move can be compared against it"
 ]
 non_negotiables: [
  "no anchor is renamed or reused; the permanence rule holds",
  "claim statements stay byte-identical through mechanical passes",
  "the raw generation moves whole; no byte changes except outward links that spw refactor rebases",
  "the quarantine keeps every file it names",
  "commits and the snapshot tag are authorized by the owner"
 ]
}

^["validation"]{
 hypotheses: [
  "H1 the moves change no anchor and no ref target: 8180 anchors before and after, and the only unresolved refs that change are the three panel refs this plan fixes",
  "H2 the receipt ledger loses nothing: every file, event, at, agent, care, and outcome tuple is recoverable from journal entries",
  "H3 receipts to the journal and a trimmed card cut at least 15 percent of the tree's lines with claim statements byte-identical",
  "H4 an agent given only the extension door and the gate adds one surface to the tree and one entry to the journal, and both pass",
  "H5 anchor-addressed refs remove about 400 thousand characters, about 8 percent of the tree"
 ]
 negative_controls: [
  "every raw shelf file is a rename into journal/2026-09-30-gemini-shelf, 100 percent except the files whose outward links were rebased",
  "the quarantine names the same nine files at their new paths",
  "the sorted list of claim statement strings is identical before and after each mechanical pass"
 ]
 demo_path: [
  "open .spw/caches/index.spw and follow the extension door",
  "add one surface to the tree and one entry to the journal in a worktree and run the gate",
  "check out the tag caches-cut/2026.09.30 and find the dated cut and the shelf as they were"
 ]
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] observe — The cut holds 439 files and 86604 lines; 68 percent of its characters sit inside strings. Path refs are 663 thousand characters, about 417 thousand of them path prefix, though anchors are already unique across the cut. The emit and provenance blocks are 14724 lines, receipts 2717 lines. 322 of about 600 concept tags occur once. The cut has no root index; the gate fails on three refs to panels nobody has written; the caches index still routes only to the raw shelf.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The owner chose samples first, then parser changes, for the syntax revision, staged under syntax-hardware-alignment, whose rule is samples before any parser change.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The owner chose a living tree with git-tag snapshots over extending the dated directory in place or opening a new dated cut per pass.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The owner asked for a directory for dated .spw files, a journal. It opens at .spw/journal at the canon root, entries named YYYY-MM-DD-slug.spw; resume notes, snapshot manifests, and receipt ledgers are its first kinds of entry.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The living tree is .spw/caches/cut; the raw shelf stays where it is, per the owner decision recorded in the caches-cut-2026-09-30 plan.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] taste — The contract is 232 lines and every rule in it is real, but an extending agent needs a door of about forty lines: where to put a surface, which exemplar to copy, which namespace to write under, which gate to run, and where its receipt goes.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] decide — The owner took @cut#src_x as the starting ref form, a root figure with a fragment; the root names the layer, so refs read @tree#src_x and @journal#entry_anchor, with both roots declared once in .spw/workspace.spw.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] decide — The owner approved caches-cut/2026.09.30 on main at 813444dc as the snapshot tag. Later snapshots of the living tree are tagged caches/YYYY.MM.DD.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] observe — Time binds unevenly: 53 surfaces mark era current, 111 carry 296 as_of lines outside provenance, and all 631 quantity cells carry an at. Season holds recurring forms (arc, retrospective protocol, festivals, fiscal and academic years, the journal template) and one dated instance, the 2026 Q4 calendar with its trail.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] revise — Putting season files in the journal moved the line: the journal is not a side folder for notes but the dated layer of the caches. A surface belongs in the tree when someone should edit it to keep it true, and in the journal when it records what was seen or made on a day and is never edited after. The tree becomes a view over the journal and the sources.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] decide — The owner chose that structure inside .spw/caches: index.spw and extend.spw at the root, tree/ for the living synthesis, journal/ for dated append-only entries. The raw generation becomes one journal entry, journal/2026-09-30-gemini-shelf, moved whole; this revises the earlier decision that the shelf stays in its topic folders, and nothing is deleted. The canon-root journal from 10:08 is dropped.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] decide — The living layer is named tree, not cut; a cut is a dated selection and this layer is not one.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] decide — Only the season instance moves: calendar-2026q4 and trails/season-2026-q4 become journal/2026-10-01-season-2026-q4; the recurring season forms stay in tree/season.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:21] implement — Tagged main at 813444dc as caches-cut/2026.09.30, annotated, local. Opened .spw/caches/journal with its contract and seven entry kinds; the resume note moved in whole as 2026-09-30-resume.spw, and the snapshot manifest is 2026-10-13-cut-snapshot.spw. The workspace declares @caches and @journal; @tree waits for the move.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:21] decide — The resume note moved in unchanged, so its not_in_this_revision frame now goes stale with the move. Under the append-only rule a new resume entry supersedes it rather than an edit; ~[root_door] writes it.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:32] implement — Moved the 13 raw topic folders and the shelf index into journal/2026-09-30-gemini-shelf with spw refactor --rename path and git mv: 196 files are pure renames, 11 jetbrains and vscode files had outward links rebased (58 edits, no conflicts), and the shelf index keeps its anchor spw_caches_index. A stub root at .spw/caches/index.spw routes the cut, the journal, and its three entries until ~[root_door].
 >>[2026-10-13 10:32] decide — Lineage strings and provenance records in the cut (708 occurrences in 159 files) keep their old .spw/caches paths: they name raw files as they stood at the tag, the gate checks only that lineage is present, and all 341 raw anchors are unique, so ~[anchor_refs_migrate] turns lineage into @journal anchor refs that no later move can break.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:32] surprise — One root-relative ref in season/index.spw cited the shelf index by anchor; spw refactor never saw it because the index moved by hand, and resolving only the journal missed it. The cut gate caught it. Resolve the whole caches root after every move, not the moved part.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:32] verify — spw resolve over .spw/caches: 10487 citations, 10479 resolve, the 8 unresolved are the known refs to unwritten panels; cut gate 3 failing as before; 212 journal files parse.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:39] implement — Moved the cut to .spw/caches/tree with spw refactor --rename path and git mv; 439 files are pure renames at the same depth, so no relative link inside them changed. Runnable command strings in the contract, recipes, practice modes, contraptions, the probe registry, and one self-source now name the tree; dated records keep the old path: an owner quote, three measurement provenance lines, and source-registry titles. The workspace declares @tree; the gate and voice docs name the tree; the caches-cut handoff carries a moved note.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:11] implement — Moved the 2026 Q4 calendar and trail into journal/2026-10-01-season-2026-q4 as calendar.spw and trail.spw with spw refactor (99 edits in 14 files, no conflicts) and git mv; the entry index names its kind, instance, and the recurring form it runs. season/index.spw and trails/index.spw no longer route the instance as a child: an ^[instances] frame cites it, a pattern for any recurring form and its dated runs.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:11] taste — season-arc.spw cites 24 anchors in the 2026 calendar as its dated examples, so next season its examples point at last year. A recurring form should name its runs through ^[instances] and keep only the dated examples it needs; deferred, recorded as taste debt.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:11] verify — tree: 437 files, 8141 anchors, 3 failing as before; the 39 anchors that left are all in the two moved files; spw resolve over .spw/caches 10482 of 10490, the 8 unresolved are the known panel refs; the new entry parses.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:16] implement — Renamed the journal kind resume to handoff and the 2026-09-30 entry to 2026-09-30-handoff.spw with spw refactor (6 edits) and git mv, as the default after the owner noted resume reads like résumé and left the word open; other surfaces keep their @resume root labels.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:22] implement — Rewrote .spw/caches/index.spw as the root: a door frame (extend, contract, vocabulary, the water exemplar), the fourteen tree classes, the journal index with its latest snapshot and handoff, and relevance tiers (lead spw, formal, physical, language_and_mind; residue spw/hosts and society/platforms; streaming kept as support). Wrote extend.spw, one screen: which layer, what to copy, names, checks, what to avoid. The contract scope names the living tree and the journal, anchors are unique across the tree, and links gain instances and journal rules. The three unwritten panels are named in ^[planned] frames instead of linked. A 2026-10-13 handoff supersedes the state frames of the 2026-09-30 note.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:22] verify — cut gate on .spw/caches/tree passes for the first time: 437 files, 0 failing, 19 size warnings; spw resolve over .spw/caches 10505 of 10505; 654 caches files parse.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:26] implement — Wrote proposals p8 to p11 into syntax-hardware-alignment with measures over the tree: p8 anchor refs remove 356395 characters across 9778 fragment refs, p9 journal receipts remove 5308 lines, p10 a lean card removes title, continuity, audience prose, and proof prose over 394 cards, p11 closed concepts drop 320 singleton tags of 645. samples/cut-surface.spw rewrites author-toolchain with all four: 97 lines and 4037 characters against 108 and 5244, statements and anchors identical, and it parses today.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:26] observe — The root-plus-fragment form parses but is no citation yet: spw select finds only the quoted form, as a file named for the root. The LSP already resolves a root followed by a path through workspace roots, and reads such forms inside strings, so p8 must narrow what it reads, not only widen it.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:36] decide — The owner chose this pass: p8 refs, refs only where they are refs, and journal-aware plugins; p10 emit derivation is out of it. p8 and refs outside strings go to citation-navigation, which owns selectPathRefs, resolve parity, anchor-line navigation, and rename rewrites; the journal-aware plugins stay here, beside the journal contract they enforce. The p9 to p11 conventions passes wait for the owner review of their samples.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:36] revise — Commits now name their proposals: concept_vocab is p11, receipts_to_journal p9, card_trim p10, anchor_refs_migrate p8; anchor_refs is dropped for citation-navigation's three root_anchor commits. New: journal_entry_lens, journal_append_only, and journal_backlinks, the last after root_anchor_refs.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:39] observe — Owner screenshots, 2026-10-13: VS Code counts incoming refs from .tmp and release/wt-pre copies that no longer exist, so journal_backlinks needs apposition-cache-granules' eviction fix before it can claim a backlink is real; nvim shows the hosts already render LSP results inline, so the journal features belong in the LSP, not in one client. .spw/index.spw now routes @caches.
}

^["open"]{
